{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795618252,"nonce":"e9QKJmNIxEcJVQK/dXQcRBBR4x0=","message":"Statics of a running class: reproduced with the 0.1.22 release binary (macOS arm64, hybrid) after a report from the hxn session, whose `hxn me dev` restarts the app, window included, when a reload is refused. hxnme systems are static functions, so adding a system always restarts.\n\nClass M has `static var n`, `static function label()` and a `main` that polls `hl.Api.checkReload()`. Each variant is swapped over a running v1:\n\n- label's body changed: reloaded.\n- a static function added before main: refused, \"$M binds different statics; a static function was added or removed\". Correct.\n- a static var added before main, with or without an initializer: refused with the same message. Wrong, no function was added.\n- a static var added after main: refused by fields.rs keep_order, \"the statics of M changed; a reload does not set up a static of a class that is running\". This is the real limit.\n\nThe wrong message comes from types.rs `incompatible()`. It compares the field index of each binding by position, and main is itself a bound static, so a variable declared ahead of it moves main's index. Comparing the bound statics by name would let the field pass give the real reason for a variable.\n\nWhat the next slice needs: match the static fields by name and keep the running order with added ones after it, as the field pass does for instances; bind an added static function's closure into the added field; decide the value of an added static variable, either zero or null, or its initializer run from a slice of the entry function the way reload/init.rs does for a new class. Not checked: whether the spare room that hlp_set_object_room allocates covers the `$` statics objects. The `statics_of` refusal in keep_order is a policy, not a room limit.\n\nThe stderr prefix \"[hot-reload] reload refused:\" (reload.rs) is read by `hxn me dev`, and crates/ash_cli/tests/hot_reload.rs matches on \"reload refused\". It stays.","files":null}]}